      "side": 1,
      "message": "This logic here is still dependent on the isSimilarity() matrix type check. When that\u0027s not the case, `computeXformedSigma` is lossy and you can\u0027t also then go back to a local-space sigma accurately either.\n\nI think what we\u0027ll need to do before we can expand the matrix types that are supported by Graphite\u0027s rrect blur is update the `drawBlurredRRect` API to take in the sigma and a flag for whether or not it\u0027s local.  \n\nFor algorithms that render with local sigma, then it can accept any matrix for the local case, but has more limited scenarios where it can handle the device sigma. For algorithms that render in device space, its\u0027 the opposite.  If we\u0027re able to support a 2D sigma, then a local algorithm also can be used in a few more non-similarity \"device sigma\" cases because an axis-aligned non-uniform scale matrix can still be represented locally.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2023,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2023,
        "endChar": 90
      },
      "revId": "cffb4710bf3e1b3f69da0d2d6555f0244f9a3147",
