      "writtenOn": "2026-08-24T14:44:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What could be causing the visual shift is a mismatch with how the LUT is defined and how we\u0027re accessing it. If it is 256 values, it probably stored x\u003d0 into texel 0 but that is sampled as float texel coord \u003d 0.5.  The final value at x\u003d1 into texel 255 is sampled as 255.5.  If we\u0027re not adjusting the normalization range to fit that here, or in how we filled out the table, then it could bias the lookup.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1870,
        "startChar": 33,
